  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Resilience in Transboundary Biodiversity Landscapes of the Mekong Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Resilience in Transboundary Biodiversity Landscapes of the Mekong Region, funded through the Mekong-Australia Partnership, focuses on seven Transboundary Biodiversity Landscapes (TBLs), critical for water security within 
entire river basins and catchments. It provides an opportunity to strengthen multi-level collaboration to 
halt biodiversity losses, improve climate change resilience and enhance economic opportunities for local 
communities and vulnerable groups.

It will nurture improved and inclusive local and cross border governance working with Community 
Protected Areas, Community Forests, agricultural cooperatives and Protected Areas management boards to restore 
shared forests, drainage corridors, farms and protected areas. Ecosystem services will be enhanced, and 
the adoption of climate-resilient and ecologically sustainable livelihoods fostered.</narrative>
  </description>
